{"name":"Mandalay Road","hex":"#a05f45","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"road","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A way used for travelling between places, originally one wide enough to allow foot passengers and horses to travel, now (US) usually one surfaced with asphalt or concrete and designed to accommodate many vehicles travelling in both directions. In the UK both senses are heard: a country road is the same as a country lane. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Roads in general as a means of travel, especially by motor vehicle."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At the venue of the opposing team or competitor; on the road.","Of or pertaining to a road bike."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/road"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mandalay","blocks":[{"text":"Mandalay is the second-largest city in Myanmar, after Yangon. It is located on the east bank of the Irrawaddy River, 631 km (392 mi) north of Yangon. In 2014, the city had a population of 1,225,553."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Mandalay_-_The_worship_of_Buddha.jpg/330px-Mandalay_-_The_worship_of_Buddha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandalay","wikidata":"Q185518"},{"title":"Road","blocks":[{"text":"A road is a thoroughfare from one place to another, primarily used for movement of traffic. Many roads are paved."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Erlangen_Bundesautobahn_73_Auffahrt_Luftbild-20230422-RM-165734.jpg/330px-Erlangen_Bundesautobahn_73_Auffahrt_Luftbild-20230422-RM-165734.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road","wikidata":"Q34442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Ku_Tho_Taw_Pagoda_%26_Sandar_Muni_Pagoda%2C_Mandalay.jpg/500px-Ku_Tho_Taw_Pagoda_%26_Sandar_Muni_Pagoda%2C_Ma